            <ArticleTitle>Prevalence of coronary artery disease, ischemic stroke, peripheral arterial disease, and coronary revascularization in older African-Americans, Asians, Hispanics, whites, men, and women.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>932-3, A7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The prevalence of coronary artery disease and of peripheral arterial disease was similar in older African-Americans, Asians, Hispanics, and whites, and the prevalence of ischemic stroke was lower in older whites than in older African-Americans and Hispanics. The prevalence of coronary revascularization in older persons with coronary artery disease was lower in African-Americans than in whites and Hispanics and was lower in women than in men.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
